# QA Re-alignment Document

## Issues

- [x] `src/data/learn/specKitAlternatives`,`intentDrivenEngineering`, `specDrivenVsIntentDrivenDevelopment`, `mcpServerForDevelopmentWorkflow`, `openSourceAgenticSdlcFramework` (rendered `out/learn/*/index.html`) -- only `claude-code-subagents-pipeline` links `/observer/`; spec-kit-alternatives links no docs page at all (two /learn links only).
  - Traces to: shell desired #3 "Each page ends with related links into the docs, /observer and the other /learn pages"; Strategy "Every page hands the reader onward: to sibling pages, the docs and /observer".
  - Misalignment: spec-gap (shell outcome says every page; brief #11 and the child specs require /observer only on the pipeline page). Decide: relax the shell outcome or add the links to the records.
  - Resolved 2026-11-27: user decided /observer/ is required only on the pipeline page; the spec relaxation is handled by the spec-writer. Docs link added to spec-kit-alternatives (`.aide intent files` -> `/docs/methodology/aide-spec/`).
- [ ] [verified-mechanically; awaiting commit] No page renders `<time>` or Article `dateModified` (byline shows "Lowmeadow LLC" only). Cause: `src/data/learn/` is untracked, so `listSitePages` has no git date. Template logic is correct (`LearnByline`, brief #6).
  - Traces to: shell desired #3 "shows its true last-updated date".
  - Misalignment: none in code; re-run the build after committing `src/data/learn` and confirm the date, `dateModified` and markdown copy appear.

## Checked clean

Layout and template (server-only, no `use client`, no review-state branch, no noindex, docs-body prose only); index order and footer `/learn/` link; breadcrumb text equals BreadcrumbList names on all pages; FAQ and glossary visible text equals FAQPage and DefinedTerm records exactly (intent-driven-engineering 4 FAQ / 5 terms, SDLC 6 / 4); glossary ids stable; no duplicate ids; all internal links resolve in `out/`; no person or TetsuKodai named; markers ([VERIFY], [NEEDS COLLECTION]) shown as-is; copy button copies the shown install string.

## Retro

The shell outcome on related links was written wider than the brief and child specs that implement it. Spec-writer should have either enumerated required links per page or kept the outcome to "sibling, docs or observer as the page needs". Dates depend on committed history, so a QA run before the first commit of `src/data/learn` cannot verify them.
